<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Aloha · Hawaii, Dec 19 – Jan 3</name>
<description>aloha.puddnsnacks.com</description>
<Folder><name>Oʻahu</name>
<Placemark><name>International Market Place, Don&#x27;s Treehouse tribute</name><description>The banyan Donn Beach built his Waikiki village around still stands, with a tribute treehouse and a plaque. It&#x27;s a mall now, so come for the tree and the plaque, not a drink. · 2330 Kalakaua Ave., Honolulu, HI 96815</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8260782,21.2783385,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Mariana Sailing Club</name><description>A 1950s tiki room on Sand Island, open since 1957. The rattan chairs came out of Don the Beachcomber&#x27;s, and the lamps are blowfish. · 50 Sand Island Access Rd., Honolulu, HI 96819</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8917776,21.3222723,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mai Tai Bar, The Royal Hawaiian</name><description>Beachfront at the Royal Hawaiian, where Trader Vic&#x27;s mai tai was first poured in Hawaii in 1953. Order the Royal Mai Tai. · 2259 Kalakaua Ave., Honolulu, HI 96815</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8289679,21.2773331,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>House Without A Key (Halekulani)</name><description>Sunset under the old kiawe tree at the Halekulani, with Hawaiian music and hula every night. · Halekulani, 2199 Kalia Rd., Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8323674,21.2779627,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hau Tree Bar, Hilton Hawaiian Village</name><description>Beach bar at the Hilton Hawaiian Village, where Harry Yee is credited with the Blue Hawaii. Some of his credits are disputed. · 2005 Kalia Rd., Honolulu, HI 96815</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8382465,21.2818802,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Skull &amp; Crown Trading Co.</name><description>A small Chinatown tiki bar from 2019. The house drink arrives on fire in a ceramic skull, made for two. · 62 N. Hotel St., Honolulu, HI 96817</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8625505,21.3119881,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tiki&#x27;s Grill &amp; Bar</name><description>Second-floor Waikiki tiki bar in the Twin Fin hotel, with a speakeasy tucked inside. · 2570 Kalakaua Ave., 2nd floor, The Twin Fin hotel, Honolulu, HI 96815</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8224714,21.2723556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Arnold&#x27;s Beach Bar &amp; Grill</name><description>A Waikiki dive with carved tikis and a cheap mai tai. · Saratoga Rd., Waikiki</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8312033,21.2812827,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Heyday at White Sands Hotel (Green Lady bar)</name><description>Mid-century Waikiki hotel bar pouring the 1944-style mai tai. A good-looking room, not a historic one. · 431 Nohonani St., Honolulu, HI 96815</description><Point><coordinates>-157.825519,21.2800825,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Polynesian Cultural Center</name><description>Polynesian villages, an imu luau and an evening show in Laie. Culture, not tiki - it has never used the word. · 55-370 Kamehameha Hwy., Laie, HI 96762</description><Point><coordinates>-157.9204432,21.640248,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Romer House Waikiki</name><description>A small Waikiki hotel reported as 18 and over. · 415 Nahua Street, Honolulu, HI 96815</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8251099,21.2793382,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Blue Note Hawaii</name><description>Waikiki&#x27;s dinner-and-show room, usually two shows a night. WAR plays Dec 30 and New Year&#x27;s Eve. · 2335 Kalakaua Ave. (Outrigger Waikiki Beachcomber), Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8276707,21.27715,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Lewers Lounge (Halekulani)</name><description>The Halekulani&#x27;s jazz lounge, home of the occasional exotica night. Waitiki 7 played here in June. · Halekulani, 2199 Kalia Rd., Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8316007,21.2780608,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hula&#x27;s Bar &amp; Lei Stand</name><description>Waikiki&#x27;s long-running LGBTQ+ bar, with Diamond Head out the window and local acoustic sets most nights. · Waikiki Grand Hotel, 134 Kapahulu Ave., 2nd floor</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8216728,21.2719838,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Duke&#x27;s Waikiki</name><description>On the sand in Waikiki, with island music twice a day. · Kalakaua Ave. (Outrigger Waikiki), Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8277917,21.2768421,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Manifest</name><description>Chinatown cafe by day, bar at night. It was the one surf-rock room on Oʻahu in 2024. · 32 N. Hotel St., Honolulu, HI 96817</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8621998,21.3115489,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hawaii Theatre</name><description>Chinatown&#x27;s restored theater, with concerts and tributes on the calendar. · 1130 Bethel St., Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8612348,21.3109813,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Senia</name><description>Chinatown, cooking built on Hawaii ingredients. The tasting menu runs Friday and Saturday at 6:30 only. · 75 N. King St., Honolulu, HI 96817</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8635678,21.3115105,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Giovanni&#x27;s Shrimp Truck (Kahuku)</name><description>The North Shore shrimp truck. Garlic scampi plate. · 56-505 Kamehameha Hwy., Kahuku, HI 96731</description><Point><coordinates>-157.9484211,21.677198,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Fumi&#x27;s Kahuku Shrimp (Ala Moana Center)</name><description>Garlic butter shrimp at the Ala Moana food court, no North Shore drive required. · Makai Market Food Court, Ala Moana Center, 1450 Ala Moana Blvd., Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8437756,21.2914679,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ono Seafood</name><description>Kapahulu poke counter. Spicy ahi, shoyu ahi or limu. · 747 Kapahulu Ave., Honolulu, HI 96816</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8140556,21.2809175,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Maguro Brothers</name><description>Shoyu ahi or ume shiso poke, in Chinatown by day and Waikiki by night. · Chinatown: 1120 Maunakea St. Waikiki: 2250 Kalakaua Ave.</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8627535,21.31264,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Boots &amp; Kimo&#x27;s Homestyle Kitchen</name><description>Kailua. Banana macadamia nut pancakes under macadamia nut sauce. · 1020 Keolu Dr., Suite D1 (Enchanted Lake Shopping Center), Kailua, HI 96734</description><Point><coordinates>-157.7292357,21.3819472,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sweet E&#x27;s Cafe</name><description>Kapahulu breakfast: stuffed French toast and macadamia nut pancakes. · 1006 Kapahulu Ave., Honolulu, HI 96816</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8135893,21.2861529,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rainbow Drive-In</name><description>Kapahulu drive-in. Mix plate or loco moco. · 3308 Kanaina Ave., Honolulu, HI 96815</description><Point><coordinates>-157.814558,21.2759435,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>KCC Farmers&#x27; Market</name><description>Saturday morning fruit, produce and prepared food at the foot of Diamond Head. · Kapiolani Community College, Parking Lot C</description><Point><coordinates>-157.801686,21.2687466,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Diamond Head State Monument (Leahi summit trail)</name><description>The crater-rim climb over Waikiki. Go at 6 a.m.</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8067896,21.2624863,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Manoa Falls Trail</name><description>The closest real rainforest to Waikiki. Muddy, rooty and busy.</description><Point><coordinates>-157.7993432,21.3422323,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kualoa Ranch Jungle Expedition</name><description>An open-air ride into a rainforest valley and its film sites.</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8372577,21.5208318,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kaneohe Bay sandbar (Ahu o Laka)</name><description>Shallow turquoise water in the middle of the bay, under the Koolau cliffs.</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8080214,21.4659568,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Lanikai and Kailua beaches, plus Kaiwa Ridge (Lanikai Pillbox) hike</name><description>Calm windward water and the Mokulua islets.</description><Point><coordinates>-157.7148121,21.3917342,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kaena Point (Natural Area Reserve)</name><description>Oʻahu&#x27;s remote western tip, with seabirds and monk seals.</description><Point><coordinates>-158.2805762,21.5744163,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Makapuu Lighthouse Trail (Kaiwi State Scenic Shoreline)</name><description>A paved coastal climb with winter whales and a view to Molokai.</description><Point><coordinates>-157.652789,21.3033867,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hau Tree, Kaimana Beach</name><description>Four courses on the sand at Kaimana Beach, from 4 p.m. on both nights. The quiet end of Waikiki. · 2863 Kalakaua Avenue, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8212682,21.2633853,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hy&#x27;s Steak House</name><description>A dark-wood steakhouse with a set Christmas dinner every night from Dec 21 to Jan 1, so it fits any trip that touches Oʻahu. · 2440 Kuhio Avenue, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8229294,21.2768529,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Stripsteak</name><description>Michael Mina&#x27;s steakhouse at International Market Place, a short walk from Donn Beach&#x27;s banyan. The set menu runs both nights. · 2330 Kalakaua Avenue, Suite 330, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8260782,21.2783385,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>53 By The Sea</name><description>A waterfront dining room in Kakaʻako with one set menu on both nights. · 53 Ahui Street, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.86093,21.2917705,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Beachhouse at the Moana</name><description>Holiday dinner menus on both nights at the Moana Surfrider, with Santa coming in by outrigger canoe on Christmas Eve. · 2365 Kalakaua Avenue, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8268852,21.276499,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tiki&#x27;s Grill &amp; Bar</name><description>The tiki bar with the Waikiki ocean view runs a Christmas surf and turf from 4 p.m. on both days. The Christmas Bar pop-up is in the same building. · 2570 Kalakaua Avenue, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8224714,21.2723556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Four Seasons Ko Olina</name><description>Ko Olina&#x27;s Christmas Eve buffet and Christmas brunch, 45 minutes to an hour from Waikiki. There&#x27;s an 18-and-over pool. · 92-1001 Olani Street, Kapolei</description><Point><coordinates>-158.125741,21.3392955,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Mer, Halekulani</name><description>Halekulani&#x27;s French room has run Christmas menus before. Nothing is posted for this year, so this one takes a phone call. · 2199 Kalia Road, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8323674,21.2779627,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Orchids, Halekulani</name><description>Brunch and dinner buffets at Halekulani on both days. In 2024 that meant oysters, snow crab, lobster tail and a carving station. The best Christmas table in Waikiki, and the first to fill. · 2199 Kalia Road, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8323674,21.2779627,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>House Without A Key, Christmas Day</name><description>Four courses under the kiawe tree at Halekulani on Christmas Day. · 2199 Kalia Road, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8323674,21.2779627,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Azure, Royal Hawaiian</name><description>A Christmas Day tasting menu on the beach at the Pink Palace. · 2259 Kalakaua Avenue, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8289679,21.2773331,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Roy&#x27;s Waikiki</name><description>Roy Yamaguchi&#x27;s room on the Waikiki Beach Walk, with a Christmas Day menu priced by the entrée. · 226 Lewers Street, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8310517,21.2792095,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Merriman&#x27;s Honolulu</name><description>Farm-to-table in Kakaʻako, with a Christmas Day prix fixe. · 1108 Auahi Street, Suite 170, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8522387,21.2937886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Plumeria Beach House, Kahala</name><description>A beachfront buffet at the Kahala, past Diamond Head. Lunch on Christmas Eve, and the full spread on Christmas Day. · 5000 Kahala Avenue, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.7728208,21.2718399,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>100 Sails, Prince Waikiki</name><description>Buffets over the yacht harbor: Christmas dinner from Dec 24 to 28, and a brunch on Christmas Day. · 100 Holomoana Street, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8400203,21.2861716,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ala Moana Center</name><description>Ala Moana and the other big malls close on Christmas Day. · 1450 Ala Moana Boulevard, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8437756,21.2914679,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Diamond Head</name><description>Diamond Head closes on Christmas Day. · Diamond Head Road, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8067896,21.2624863,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pearl Harbor visitor center</name><description>The Pearl Harbor visitor center closes on Christmas Day. · 1 Arizona Memorial Place, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.9384488,21.3674843,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Polynesian Cultural Center</name><description>The Polynesian Cultural Center closes on Christmas Day. · 55-370 Kamehameha Highway, Laie</description><Point><coordinates>-157.9204432,21.640248,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Christmas Bar at Tiki&#x27;s</name><description>A Christmas bar pop-up inside Tiki&#x27;s, back every year. Last year it ran until Dec 30. · 2570 Kalakaua Avenue, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8224714,21.2723556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Prince Waikiki holiday bar</name><description>The Prince&#x27;s holiday bar, home to Sippin&#x27; Santa, the tiki Christmas pop-up, in past years. · 100 Holomoana Street, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8400203,21.2861716,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>MAKANA at the ʻAlohilani</name><description>A 21-and-over holiday pop-up in the Oceanarium Lounge at the ʻAlohilani. Last year it was open on Christmas Eve and Christmas night. · 2490 Kalakaua Avenue, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8257486,21.2760811,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Honolulu City Lights</name><description>The big tree and Shaka Santa at Honolulu Hale, free, from Dec 5. Last year it ran through Dec 31. · 530 South King Street, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8570082,21.3052679,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Christmas Eve at Halekulani</name><description>Halekulani&#x27;s Christmas Eve: Santa arrives at 3:30 and a holiday reception runs on the Hau Terrace from 5 to 6. · 2199 Kalia Road, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8323674,21.2779627,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kawaiahaʻo Church</name><description>The coral-block church from 1842, across the street from the City Lights. This year&#x27;s Christmas Eve service time isn&#x27;t posted. · 957 Punchbowl Street, Honolulu</description><Point><coordinates>-157.8578157,21.3043456,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Honolulu (HNL)</name><description>Southwest flies here.</description><Point><coordinates>-157.9184436,21.3211445,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Maui</name>
<Placemark><name>South Shore Tiki Lounge</name><description>Kihei&#x27;s tiki lounge, with an all-day happy hour and live music. · 1913-J S. Kihei Rd., Kihei, HI 96753</description><Point><coordinates>-156.4516573,20.7322335,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Old Lahaina Luau</name><description>The traditional one: hula and history, no fire knife, and drinks for 21 and over. Lahaina&#x27;s Front Street reopened Aug 1. · 1251 Front Street, Lahaina, HI</description><Point><coordinates>-156.684978,20.886018,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Feast at Mokapu</name><description>A plated, oceanfront luau at the Andaz in Wailea, with holiday menus for Christmas and New Year&#x27;s Eve. · 3550 Wailea Alanui Drive, Wailea, HI 96753</description><Point><coordinates>-156.4411739,20.6929816,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hotel Wailea, Relais &amp; Chateaux</name><description>Maui&#x27;s only adults-only hotel. Everyone is 18 or older. · 555 Kaukahi Street, Wailea, HI 96753</description><Point><coordinates>-156.4322156,20.6774754,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Branches (Royal Lahaina Resort)</name><description>Free Hawaiian and island music nightly in Kaanapali, 6 to 9 p.m. · Royal Lahaina Resort &amp; Bungalows, 2780 Kekaa Dr., Lahaina</description><Point><coordinates>-156.6919385,20.9311369,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casanova</name><description>Upcountry in Makawao. Its Aloha Music Series plays Sunday afternoons. · 1188 Makawao Ave., Makawao, HI 96768</description><Point><coordinates>-156.3104895,20.8536105,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kahale&#x27;s</name><description>Kihei&#x27;s dive bar since 1994, with live bands and a long happy hour. It says it&#x27;s open 365 days. · Kihei</description><Point><coordinates>-156.451483,20.7324819,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mama&#x27;s Fish House</name><description>Maui&#x27;s hardest table to get. Whether it&#x27;s open on Christmas isn&#x27;t posted, and it books up to 18 months out. · 799 Poho Place, Paia</description><Point><coordinates>-156.3669784,20.9290567,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Geste Shrimp Truck</name><description>Kahului shrimp truck: garlic or spicy pineapple shrimp. · Kahului. Two addresses are listed, so check the map before you drive.</description><Point><coordinates>-156.447776,20.8883688,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Like Poke?</name><description>Kahului poke truck near the airport. The furikake bowl. · 591 Haleakala Hwy., Kahului, HI</description><Point><coordinates>-156.447776,20.8883688,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>South Maui Fish Company</name><description>Kihei truck: ahi poke bowl or fish tacos. · 1794 S. Kihei Rd., Kihei, HI</description><Point><coordinates>-156.4535938,20.7352876,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sam Sato&#x27;s</name><description>Wailuku noodle house: house-made saimin and noodle plates, and BBQ sticks. · 1750 Wili Pa Loop, Wailuku, HI 96793</description><Point><coordinates>-156.500452,20.8931173,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cafe Mambo</name><description>Paia all-day spot: pancakes, burritos and burgers. · 30 Baldwin Ave., Paia, HI 96779</description><Point><coordinates>-156.3805579,20.9155034,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Upcountry Farmers Market</name><description>Saturday morning Upcountry Maui produce and fruit in Pukalani. · Kulamalu Town Center, near the football fields</description><Point><coordinates>-156.329557,20.8210492,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Haleakala summit sunrise</name><description>Sunrise above the clouds at 10,023 feet, then down Sliding Sands into the crater.</description><Point><coordinates>-156.2498143,20.7151133,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pipiwai Trail to Waimoku Falls (Kipahulu District)</name><description>Maui&#x27;s best jungle hike: a banyan, a bamboo forest and a 400-foot waterfall.</description><Point><coordinates>-156.0567179,20.6740805,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Iao Valley State Monument</name><description>A short loop into a lush valley under the Iao Needle.</description><Point><coordinates>-156.5471216,20.8805863,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Makena State Park (Oneloa / Big Beach)</name><description>A wide, wild golden beach.</description><Point><coordinates>-156.4472714,20.633795,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Waianapanapa State Park</name><description>Black sand, sea caves and a lava-coast trail on the Road to Hana.</description><Point><coordinates>-156.0021226,20.7865498,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hotel Wailea</name><description>Five courses above the sea at the adults-only hotel, on both nights. The most grown-up Christmas dinner on any island. · 555 Kaukahi Street, Wailea</description><Point><coordinates>-156.4322156,20.6774754,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Spago and Ferraro&#x27;s, Four Seasons Maui</name><description>Spago and Ferraro&#x27;s add Christmas specials to the regular menus in Wailea. · 3900 Wailea Alanui Drive, Wailea</description><Point><coordinates>-156.4418943,20.6801737,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cane &amp; Canoe, Montage Kapalua</name><description>Kapalua&#x27;s oceanfront room serves Christmas dinners on both nights. · 1 Bay Drive, Kapalua</description><Point><coordinates>-156.664678,21.0014676,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Merriman&#x27;s Kapalua</name><description>Merriman&#x27;s on the Kapalua point, with a Christmas prix fixe. A half lobster is $40 more. · 1 Bay Club Place, Kapalua</description><Point><coordinates>-156.6671208,20.9984638,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ritz-Carlton Kapalua</name><description>Christmas Day dinners at the Ritz-Carlton up in Kapalua. · 1 Ritz-Carlton Drive, Kapalua</description><Point><coordinates>-156.6541367,20.9999919,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Haleakala</name><description>Haleakala on Christmas Day. The park&#x27;s hours page shows no closure, but that&#x27;s worth a call. · Haleakala Highway</description><Point><coordinates>-156.1324301,20.6991334,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Drums of the Pacific, Hyatt Maui</name><description>Drums of the Pacific, the Hyatt Regency&#x27;s luau in Kaanapali, takes bookings for Christmas Day. Over Christmas the resort leans family. · 200 Nohea Kai Drive, Lahaina</description><Point><coordinates>-156.6916397,20.9124823,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kahului (OGG)</name><description>Southwest flies here.</description><Point><coordinates>-156.4340476,20.8956979,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Big Island</name>
<Placemark><name>Don the Beachcomber Restaurant &amp; Don&#x27;s Mai Tai Bar, Royal Kona Resort</name><description>Oceanfront in Kailua-Kona with ten mai tai versions. The Don the Beachcomber name came with Hawaii rights the resort bought in 2005, not from Donn Beach. · 75-5852 Alii Dr., Kailua-Kona, HI 96740</description><Point><coordinates>-155.99039,19.632117,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Voyagers of the Pacific</name><description>Kona&#x27;s show luau, ending with a Samoan fire knife dance. Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday and Friday. · 75-5852 Alii Drive, Kailua-Kona, HI</description><Point><coordinates>-155.99039,19.632117,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
